{"uid":"d34edc8d02aa899b","name":"test_an_unrelated_detail_refresh_preserves_the_in_progress_draft","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub_parked#test_an_unrelated_detail_refresh_preserves_the_in_progress_draft","historyId":"04fdc21752e3e973da4cfb746d2ef0b0","time":{"start":1791983966565,"stop":1791983989237,"duration":22672},"description":"cure-01-01-5 (B.3-B.5, adopted #270 D.14): the review's own live\n    probe found that ANY fresh `events.jsonl` entry -- even one with\n    nothing to do with the parked question, `notification.failed` here --\n    moved the run-detail `ETag` and re-rendered the panel from scratch,\n    silently wiping the operator's own in-progress draft name/text. Pinned\n    through the REAL background poll (never a synthetic `renderParkedPanel`\n    call): the draft is typed, an unrelated event is appended on disk, and\n    the poll is given real time to observe the moved `ETag` before the\n    draft is asserted still exactly what was typed.","descriptionHtml":"<p>cure-01-01-5 (B.3-B.5, adopted #270 D.14): the review's own live<br />\nprobe found that ANY fresh <code>events.jsonl</code> entry -- even one with<br />\nnothing to do with the parked question, <code>notification.failed</code> here --<br />\nmoved the run-detail <code>ETag</code> and re-rendered the panel from scratch,<br />\nsilently wiping the operator's own in-progress draft name/text. Pinned<br />\nthrough the REAL background poll (never a synthetic <code>renderParkedPanel</code><br />\ncall): the draft is typed, an unrelated event is appended on disk, and<br />\nthe poll is given real time to observe the moved <code>ETag</code> before the<br />\ndraft is asserted still exactly what was typed.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791983048288,"stop":1791983048289,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],